WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
You own a used car.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.270
It runs perfectly: no faults,

3
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.180
no nasty surprises.

4
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.450
You know what it is worth,

5
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.510
so you ask a fair price.

6
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.640
But the offers come in low.

7
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.400
Lower than the car is worth,

8
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.260
again and again.

9
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.120
So why can a used car that runs perfectly

10
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.670
be hard to sell for what it is worth?

11
00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.750
In this mission, you'll work
out exactly what a careful

12
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.340
buyer is willing to pay,

13
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.940
step by step.

14
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.910
Then you'll use a graph lab:

15
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.060
slide the share of good cars
and watch the market respond.

16
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.320
Your mission: explain why
a good car can struggle

17
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.880
to fetch a fair price.
